## FEATURE 1 – REWARD FULFILLMENT MANAGEMENT

### Objective

Currently, customers can redeem rewards using their points.

Now implement the complete reward fulfillment workflow so the factory admin can manage rewards after redemption.

### Customer Side

Add:
- Reward redemption confirmation.
- Unique order/reference ID.
- Fulfillment status.
- Redemption date.
- Expected delivery date.
- Delivery details.
- Tracking number.
- Fulfillment timeline.
- Reward delivery status notifications.

Customer should see the following statuses:

1. Pending
2. Approved
3. Processing
4. Shipped
5. Delivered
6. Rejected

Add fulfillment tracking to the existing Redemption History page.

Customers must only access their own fulfillment records.

### Admin Side

Create a Reward Fulfillment Management page.

Admin can:
- View all reward fulfillment requests.
- Search by customer name and order ID.
- Filter by status.
- Approve requests.
- Reject requests with a reason.
- Update processing status.
- Add tracking numbers.
- Add admin notes.
- Mark rewards as shipped or delivered.
- View fulfillment history.

### Backend

- Extend the existing redemption architecture.
- Store fulfillment information in MongoDB.
- Validate allowed status transitions.
- Protect admin-only operations.
- Ensure customers cannot access another customer's records.
- Preserve existing points deduction and reward redemption logic.
- Prevent duplicate fulfillment processing.

Document reward fulfillment assumptions in ASSUMPTIONS.md.

