## FEATURE 2 – ADMIN AUDIT TRAIL

### Objective

The factory owner should be able to monitor important administrative activities.

### Record These Activities

- Product created, updated or deleted.
- Reward created, updated or deleted.
- Customer blocked or unblocked.
- Reward approved or rejected.
- Fulfillment status changed.
- Product code batches generated.
- Fraud case reviewed.
- System settings updated.

### Audit Log Information

Each record should contain:

- Admin ID.
- Admin identifier.
- Action type.
- Module name.
- Target record ID.
- Activity description.
- Timestamp.
- Relevant metadata.

Never store passwords, JWT tokens, API keys or other secrets in audit records.

### Admin UI

Create an Admin Audit Trail page with:

- Activity table.
- Search.
- Date filters.
- Admin filters.
- Module filters.
- Action filters.
- Pagination.
- Activity details.

### Backend

- Create an AuditLog model.
- Create reusable audit logging functionality.
- Integrate it into relevant existing admin operations.
- Protect audit APIs using admin authorization.
- Prevent customers from accessing audit logs.
- Ensure important actions are logged consistently.

Document the audit logging architecture.

