## FEATURE 3 – ADVANCED FRAUD INVESTIGATION

### Objective

The existing project already has basic Fraud Monitoring.

Enhance it into a more advanced fraud investigation and risk management system.

Do not create a duplicate fraud monitoring module.

### Risk Scoring

Implement a transparent rule-based risk score.

Consider:
- Repeated invalid code attempts.
- Duplicate redemption attempts.
- Suspicious request frequency.
- Repeated suspicious activities.
- Existing fraud logs.

Display a risk level:

- Low Risk
- Medium Risk
- High Risk
- Critical Risk

The score must be based on documented rules, not falsely described as AI-powered.

### Investigation Management

Admin should be able to:

- View suspicious customers.
- View suspicious activities.
- View related product code information.
- View fraud attempt history.
- Review suspicious events.
- Add investigation notes.
- Mark cases as Under Review.
- Mark cases as Resolved.
- Mark cases as False Positive.
- Block or unblock customers when authorized.

### Admin UI

Enhance the existing Fraud Monitoring page.

Add:
- Risk score cards.
- Suspicious activity table.
- Risk-level filters.
- Customer investigation details.
- Fraud history.
- Investigation notes.
- Case status management.

### Backend

- Extend existing FraudLog functionality.
- Avoid duplicate fraud records.
- Use documented risk scoring rules.
- Protect admin investigation APIs.
- Ensure all investigation actions are recorded in Audit Trail.

Document fraud scoring assumptions in ASSUMPTIONS.md.

