## FEATURE 4 – REWARD CAMPAIGN MANAGEMENT

### Objective

Allow the factory owner to create promotional campaigns to increase customer loyalty.

### Admin Features

Admin can:

- Create campaigns.
- Edit campaigns.
- Activate campaigns.
- Pause campaigns.
- End campaigns.
- Delete eligible campaigns.
- Configure campaign start and end dates.
- Select eligible products.
- Configure campaign reward multipliers.
- Set campaign eligibility conditions.
- View campaign performance.

### Campaign Types

Support:

1. Double Points Campaign.
2. Bonus Points Campaign.
3. Festival Campaign.
4. Limited-Time Campaign.
5. New Customer Campaign.

### Customer Side

Display:

- Active campaigns.
- Campaign description.
- Start and end date.
- Eligible products.
- Available bonus points.
- Campaign status.

### Example

Factory owner launches:

DIWALI SPECIAL – DOUBLE POINTS

A normal product code provides 100 points.

During an eligible campaign, the customer receives 200 points.

The campaign must apply only when its conditions are satisfied.

### Backend

- Create a Campaign model.
- Implement campaign management APIs.
- Validate campaign dates and eligibility.
- Prevent duplicate bonus point credits.
- Integrate campaign calculations with the existing code redemption workflow.
- Ensure point transactions accurately record campaign bonuses.
- Prevent campaign stacking unless explicitly configured.

Document campaign rules and assumptions.

