## FEATURE 5 – CUSTOMER SUPPORT & DISPUTE MANAGEMENT

### Objective

Customers should be able to report problems related to codes, points and rewards.

### Customer Side

Add a Support Center.

Customers can create support tickets for:

- Invalid product code.
- Already redeemed code.
- Points not credited.
- Reward redemption problem.
- Missing reward delivery.
- Incorrect fulfillment status.
- Other issues.

Each ticket should contain:

- Ticket ID.
- Customer ID.
- Issue category.
- Subject.
- Description.
- Related product code, if applicable.
- Related redemption ID, if applicable.
- Creation date.
- Current status.

Ticket statuses:

1. Open
2. In Progress
3. Waiting for Customer
4. Resolved
5. Closed

Customers can:

- Create tickets.
- View their tickets.
- View ticket status.
- Reply to support messages.
- View resolution details.

### Admin Side

Create a Support & Dispute Management page.

Admin can:

- View all support tickets.
- Search tickets.
- Filter by category and status.
- View customer information.
- Reply to customers.
- Add internal notes.
- Update ticket status.
- Resolve disputes.
- View complete ticket history.

### Backend

- Create SupportTicket and related message functionality.
- Implement customer and admin support APIs.
- Enforce ownership permissions.
- Validate ticket status transitions.
- Persist all messages in MongoDB.
- Record important admin actions in Audit Trail.

Document support workflow assumptions.

